00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.700
- How did it happen?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.400
- So I became homeless

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.190
after I left home to escape some abuse

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.530
at the hands of an extended family member.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.300
And I befriended some people

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.400
who seemed like wonderful people.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.650
And then these two gentlemen
began speaking to me

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:17.790
about selling sex as a
way of making a living.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:22.790
I rejected their offers
because I was only a teenager,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.270
and later those two men came and took me

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.770
and put me in the trunk of the car

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.150
and drove off into the night,

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.880
and that was the beginning
of my exploitation.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.914
- How old were you when this happened?

00:01:34.914 --> 00:01:38.850
- Yes, so I was 16 years old
when I first was exploited,

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:39.960
and then I wasn't able

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.150
to get out of my trafficking experience

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.100
until after I was 17.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.440
- How many abusers did you have?

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.750
- Well I had two main traffickers,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.480
and then as far as the
people who purchased me,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.990
which would be the folks who
abused me day in and day out,

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.930
I had over 24,000 buyers.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.300
The age range of the men who bought me

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.430
would be anywhere from
their early twenties

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.680
up into like elderly men.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.370
But the typical age of a buyer
is the middle-aged white male

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.380
usually with a six-figure income.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.580
- What kind of abuse did
you endure during your time?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.640
- I mean there was really
all kinds of abuse.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.310
There was, of course, sexual
abuse, physical abuse,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.080
psychological abuse.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.180
A lot of it was just also unpredictable.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.640
So you might have gotten paid with change,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.770
and I would give the change
over to the trafficker,

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.440
and then suddenly change
is not acceptable,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.835
and now I'm being beaten

00:02:32.835 --> 00:02:35.913
with the change inside of a pillowcase

00:02:35.913 --> 00:02:38.850
to let me know not to
ever take change again.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:42.210
And then the next night I turn
down a buyer who has change

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.420
and then I would get beaten
because I didn't accept money.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.360
So it was really all
about keeping us confused.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.580
- How was your living condition

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.800
during the time they kept you?

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.270
- Our living conditions were terrible.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.960
We lived in a terrible apartment.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.570
Had literal mold covering
all of the walls.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.940
We had no furniture except for one bed,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.320
but you couldn't sleep in the bed.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.816
We also weren't allowed food or water.

00:03:06.816 --> 00:03:09.060
We weren't allowed to
pick out our own clothing.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.680
We weren't allowed to bathe.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.620
We didn't have towels, soap, toothbrushes.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.880
We had nothing.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:15.930
- Was there ever a point

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.570
where you thought this
was gonna be forever?

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.580
And what got you through day by day?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.190
- Yeah, so I thought every single day

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.990
that this was going to be forever.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.950
And so I really just
lived moment to moment.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.570
I frequently dissociated.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:34.080
That was probably one of the
biggest savers for my brain.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.380
I am very grateful for
my ability to dissociate

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.800
and remove me from situations

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.340
that would have otherwise
broke me mentally.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.163
- Did you try to seek help from anyone?

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.546
- So I did not try to seek help

00:03:47.546 --> 00:03:50.130
while I was being trafficked.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.850
One, because they had
drilled it into our heads

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.610
that if we went to the police,
that we would be arrested

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:59.490
because we were criminals,
we were prostitutes.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.380
- What do you think
about the people who paid

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.500
or got access to you
through the traffickers?

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.360
Do you think they knew what was going on,

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.760
and what do you think
they were doing there?

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.948
- I don't think that all the buyers

00:04:10.948 --> 00:04:13.470
were aware I was being trafficked,

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:17.010
though a lot of them did
ask questions about my pimp.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.810
So they definitely knew

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.000
that I was under somebody else's control,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.600
and that my profits would
be going to another person.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.970
Any buyer who wants to help you,

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.010
that just means that
they wanna take you home,

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.110
and make you their personal slave.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.480
And that didn't really
seem like a good idea.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.370
As far as what I think about buyers,

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.190
it takes a certain level of entitlement.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.690
Whatever is going on in their life,

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:43.110
whether it's under the
guise of being lonely

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.780
or having sex as a quote unquote need,

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.240
versus what it actually is, it's a want.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.340
You know, air and water
and food are a need.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.960
They give themselves permission.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.260
So to objectify and
dehumanize me on that level

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.930
in order to make me an
object of pleasure for them,

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.680
that's not somebody who I can
have empathy or sympathy for.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.510
- How do you feel about sex work?

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.920
- So I personally do not
believe that sex work is work.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.070
I think the lowest statistic
that I've read was 87%

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.350
of people who are in exploitation,

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.030
even if they're choosing to be there,

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.460
that they feel trapped
and there's not a way out,

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.690
and so they continue.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:22.590
And if somebody feels trapped,
is that really consent?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:26.580
If somebody would rather say
"No," is that consensual?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.050
And are we okay with that?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.580
- How did you escape?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.300
- Yeah, so we would frequently
move hotels and hotel rooms,

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.988
and a hotel employee saw
this group of young girls

00:05:36.988 --> 00:05:40.740
getting in a car with
these two older gentlemen,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.360
thought something didn't seem right,

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.300
and so they contacted law enforcement.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.030
Unfortunately, the state that I was in

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.520
is one of half of the states

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.950
that charged children with prostitution.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.910
So even though I was
abducted and trafficked,

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.040
the police arrested me.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.860
I was arrested and
charged with prostitution

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.540
and aggravated money laundering

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.010
for taking money from the buyers

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.898
and giving it to my traffickers.

00:06:07.898 --> 00:06:11.580
- And did they offer any
resources to help you or anything?

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:12.413
Or...

00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:13.410
- No.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.240
- How long were you in prison?

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.590
- Yeah, so I was held

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:20.040
for 40 days in this
maximum-security facility.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.640
My two traffickers each served
10 days for their crimes.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.020
They took plea deals.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.560
My main abductor, the one who
I spent the most time with,

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:29.770
he has never been to prison,

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.040
and he is not a registered sex offender,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.443
as he has not seen as a
danger to the community.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.170
- Oh my gosh.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:40.650
When you returned and you
were able to come home,

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.860
how did your family and
friends react or treat you?

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.990
- So my family didn't learn

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.090
the true story about what had happened

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:52.020
until after I learned the true
story of what had happened.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.330
'Cause this wasn't
something that I recognized.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.300
When you're a child and
you have traffickers

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.480
that are painting the illusion
that you're making choices,

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.360
and then to be arrested, and
then to have been labeled,

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.594
and to serve time, all of those things

00:07:05.594 --> 00:07:09.570
told me that I was a
perpetrator and not a victim.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.400
So when I came home, what
I came home to was a family

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.820
who believed that I was a criminal,

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.265
and so I was treated as very lucky

00:07:16.265 --> 00:07:18.425
to have a space to even come to

00:07:18.425 --> 00:07:20.670
after what I had decided to do.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.470
And so it wasn't until I had gone

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.870
through a pretty significant
amount of therapy

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.970
that I could speak to my parents about it.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:31.920
- Do you find yourself
like a lot more hyper aware

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:35.550
of your surroundings
today compared to before?

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.040
- I am very hypervigilant

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.080
because I was taken after
a knock on the door.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.030
If somebody knocks on my
door, I don't answer it.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.680
Like to this day, I don't even get up.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.870
I'm not even the least bit curious

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.880
about what's on the
other side of that door.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.890
