00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.870
and it's been years since it's happened,

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:55.230
would you consider yourself
a victim or a survivor?

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.430
- Both.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.800
I am not ashamed of being a victim.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.230
I have nothing to be ashamed of.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.857
I was a victim of two people

00:08:03.857 --> 00:08:07.470
who purposefully perpetrated
these crimes against myself.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:09.420
And I'm also a survivor,

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.760
because I'm not currently
in that situation.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.440
And I can speak to the other side

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.170
of what it's like to come
out of that situation.

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:19.830
- If you can write a letter
to yourself from that time,

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.170
from like the beginning,
what would you write,

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:26.460
and how would you encourage
that version of you,

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:27.583
that part of you?

00:08:27.583 --> 00:08:31.650
- I think really just recognizing
that it wasn't my fault.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.450
Even to this day, I still have a hard time

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.880
having empathy for little me.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.513
But then when it comes to
old me, when I think about me

00:08:38.513 --> 00:08:41.400
when I don't have physical
control of my body,

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:44.430
when once again I am at
the mercy of other people,

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.920
that scares the heck out of me.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.190
And so I try to hold empathy
and space for young me.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.290
And then I really think about encouraging

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:55.524
the older version of myself
who's going to have have

00:08:55.524 --> 00:08:59.250
all of these triggers and
a real loss of control.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:03.240
- This is very special to me
to be able to talk with you.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.270
I was assaulted some years ago,

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.270
so I can't even comprehend
your story and your experience,

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:17.570
knowing how that experience
has shaped and changed my life.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.360
Thank you again for sharing.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.280
I really so appreciate it.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.483
- What makes you happy?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.370
- Life.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.173
I mean, I shouldn't be alive.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.573
I'm grateful for every day.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:32.673
- Oh, that hit.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.220
Sorry, I'm like kind of getting
emotional in this interview

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.360
just 'cause I've been
through like a situation,

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.100
and so I just feel like

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.860
it's bringing me a lot of
clarity talking to you,

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.270
even though like it's been hard for me

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.980
to ask certain questions.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.400
But I'm really thankful that
you're sharing your story,

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.640
'cause I feel like a lot of
people need to hear about this,

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:00.360
and I really appreciate
you just for speaking out.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.280
- Yes, thank you so much for being here.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.330
What a warrior you are.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.890
Look at you.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:05.723
- Thank you.

00:10:05.723 --> 00:10:08.073
- What's your favorite
part about life today?

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.950
- I mean, really all of it.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:15.950
I love my life now so much.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.080
I have an insane amount of friends.

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:24.080
And my children are the
coolest people I have ever met.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.010
I don't know why I'm so lucky.

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:28.710
Being seen for myself, you
know, for the first time,

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:31.890
in this phase of my life
is just such a gift.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.860
It's such a gift to feel
genuine love for who I am.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.693
- Wow.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.610
I'm happy that it's over for you,

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:42.352
and you get to like live your
life, and I'm here for you,

00:10:42.352 --> 00:10:45.241
and I can't wait to meet
you on the other side.

00:10:45.241 --> 00:10:46.328
Hi.
- You did amazing.

00:10:46.328 --> 00:10:47.364
- Thank you so much.

00:10:47.364 --> 00:10:48.690
- Oh my gosh, you're so brave

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.690
for coming and talking about this stuff.

00:10:51.604 --> 00:10:53.513
I'm glad you're here.

00:10:53.513 --> 00:10:55.083
You did good.

00:10:55.083 --> 00:10:55.953
It's okay.

